<section class="panel" aria-label="Grade 3 Unit 4 Lesson 13 teen products source"><h2>Estimate: 4×18</h2><p>Students choose and explain too-low/about-right/too-high estimates, not a unique answer list. Exact72; nearby benchmark4×20=80.</p><h2>Source farmers-market eggs: seven dozen</h2><div role="img" aria-label="Independent carton layout showing twelve eggs, six on each of two rows" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,36px);width:max-content;border:1px solid;padding:8px"><span style="padding:4px">◯</span><span style="padding:4px">◯</span><span style="padding:4px">◯</span><span style="padding:4px">◯</span><span style="padding:4px">◯</span><span style="padding:4px">◯</span><span style="padding:4px">◯</span><span style="padding:4px">◯</span><span style="padding:4px">◯</span><span style="padding:4px">◯</span><span style="padding:4px">◯</span><span style="padding:4px">◯</span></div><p>One original carton contains12 eggs. Seven dozen=7×12=84 eggs. The independent carton above is not publisher artwork.</p><h2>Source five rows of15 chairs</h2><p>5×15=5×10+5×5=50+25=75 chairs. Design a poster explaining a matching drawing; a teacher compares multiple strategies during the original partner gallery walk.</p><h2>Source rectangular table top</h2><div role="img" aria-label="Rectangular table with side lengths 4 feet and 16 feet, area 64 square feet" style="border:2px solid currentColor;width:320px;height:80px;display:grid;place-items:center">4 ft × 16 ft = 64 ft²</div><p>The original source image was read, but the picture and protected Bags of Oranges Cool-down have not been copied. Gallery walk and estimates require teacher review. <a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-4/lesson-13/lesson.html">2021 teacher source</a></p></section>
